<BaseLayout title="About | Eric Bello" description="Background, credentials, and technical direction for Eric Bello.">
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="page-context">Background & credentials</p>
    <h1>Technical range with a systems focus.</h1>
    <p>I’m an IT professional with a B.S. in Computer Engineering and certifications in CompTIA Network+, CompTIA Security+, and AWS Cloud Practitioner. I’m focused on IT support and infrastructure work now, with a clear direction toward security operations.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-shell shell ">
    <div class="content-section facts" id="credentials">
      <h2>At a glance</h2>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Education</dt><dd>B.S. Computer Engineering, Florida International University</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Certifications</dt><dd>CompTIA Network+, CompTIA Security+, AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Technical focus</dt><dd>IT support, infrastructure, cloud, identity, and security operations</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Miami, Florida</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>My background spans IT operations, cloud infrastructure, and web development, shaped by real world experience running a small business, doing freelance technical work, and building hands on projects from scratch. That range has made me adaptable and practical, especially in environments where you have to diagnose problems and keep moving.</p>
      <p>I’m drawn to work with a clear technical outcome: keeping systems healthy, diagnosing what is broken, improving access and reliability, or building something that did not exist before.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Infrastructure & identity</h2>
      <p>I built a Windows Server lab environment with Active Directory, DNS, DHCP, organizational units, Group Policy, security groups, and practical identity administration workflows. The environment gives me repeatable hands on practice with the kinds of user, policy, access, and network issues that appear in real IT environments.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Cloud & automation</h2>
      <p>I built and deployed a serverless application on AWS using S3, CloudFront, Lambda, DynamoDB, and API Gateway. The infrastructure is managed with CloudFormation and AWS SAM, with deployment automated through GitHub Actions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Security direction</h2>
      <p>Security is where I’m heading. I hold CompTIA Security+ and have applied security fundamentals throughout my lab work, including access control, Group Policy enforcement, MFA, and patch management. I continue building security operations skills through hands on labs and independent study.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
